        "#Image smoothing : no sudden changes in intensity of pixels\n",
        "#1. Object removal\n",
        "#2. Sharpness decrease : when sudden changes are there then image is sharp...sudden changes like ek row puri black then suddenly agli row is light intensity\n",
        "#3. Finer details hide : edge info loss\n",
        "\n",
        "#we are loosing information hence storage memoery used less\n",
        "#textual info ya phir finer details not needed in every image because sometimes we just need to count the objects and we dont finer details\n",
        "#so it depends do we need finer details or not\n",
        "\n",
        "#smoothing se sometimes noise also removed, not everytime but in some applications\n",
        "\n",
        "#salt and paper noise : when bahut saare dots come...jaise phele time ke tv's mein\n",
        "#for that we can have diff types of filters to remove that noise\n",
        "\n",
        "#Smoothening filters(spacial) : spacial means they work on individual pixels i.e ek ek pixel par they work\n",
        "#A. Linear\n",
        "#1. Box\n",
        "#2. Weight Avg.\n",
        "#3. Gaussian\n",
        "\n",
        "#B. Non-Linear\n",
        "#1. Median\n",
        "#2. Max\n",
        "#3. Min\n",
        "\n",
        "#Lets we have some image\n",
        "# 1 8 8 0 7\n",
        "# 4 7 9 5 7\n",
        "# 5 4 6 8 6\n",
        "# 4 2 0 1 5\n",
        "# 0 1 0 2 0\n",
        "\n",
        "#these filters works in shape of mask\n",
        "#mask is matrix i.e sq matrix 3*3 or 5*5\n",
        "#jitni finer details u wanna work utna chotta mask but utna jiyada time lagega\n",
        "\n",
        "#1. Box\n",
        "#make a box in center of image... i.e area of image under consideration\n",
        "#all components are of same value in a box\n",
        "#iska mask is following\n",
        "# 1 1 1\n",
        "# 1 1 1\n",
        "# 1 1 1\n",
        "# all components are divided outside of mask by 9 since sum of all components of mask is 9\n",
        "#component wise multiply window and mask and then add...divide by 9 = 4.66 almost 5\n",
        "#change center of window as 6...i.e pixel under consideration\n",
        "#image blur ho gyi hai\n",
        "\n",
        "#2. Weighted Avg.\n",
        "# gives more or less weight to pixels\n",
        "#lets take less weight wala exmaple\n",
        "#iska mask is following\n",
        "# 1 2 1\n",
        "# 2 4 2\n",
        "# 1 2 1\n",
        "# all components are divided by 16 outside since sum is 16 in mask\n",
        "#the mask is not fixed..now since center wala pixel of input par we are gonna work so mask mein osko sabse jiyada weight de diya\n",
        "\n",
        "#diff in box and weighted avg is\n",
        "#box mein sab equally contribute kr rhe hai...khud bhi neighbouring bhi\n",
        "#weightage mein we can decide khud ki importance deni hai....i.e khud ki value retain krni hai ya neighbouring pixels ko jiyada importance deni and onke acc change krna hai\n",
        "\n",
        "#3. Gaussian\n",
        "# it has an equation\n",
        "# G(x,y) = (1/2*pi*sigma^2)*e^((-n^2 + y^2)/2*sigma^2)\n",
        "#sigma is sd\n",
        "#It is used to blur edges and reduce contrast\n",
        "#It is similar to median filter but its faster\n",
        "\n",
        "#4. Median\n",
        "# part of image under consideration mein values ko write in increasing order\n",
        "# jo median value hogi osmein take that image\n",
        "# change the pixel to be changed in window = median of window under consideration\n",
        "\n",
        "#5. Min\n",
        "# min value se replace in window under consideration\n",
        "\n",
        "#6. Max\n",
        "# max value se replace in window under consideration"
